  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R1, R2, and R5 establish the use of MTPs in multicomponent refractory alloys, while R7 shows that MTP-type models can reproduce DFT-derived energetics in another alloy system. These records therefore support the general idea of replacing a conventional empirical potential with a DFT-trained machine-learning potential. However, none describes liquid-phase MTP training for TaVCrW, free-energy perturbation as a replacement for thermodynamic integration, convergence through low MTP–DFT energy-difference variance, or the combined electronic-DOS and solid-state SRO corrections to melting. Thus the literature points in the right general direction, but reconstructing the specific accelerated melting-free-energy method would require substantial new ideas."
}
